From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:02:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME: do not open software decoders for more
 than 8 bits

The frames of software decoders are only supported in 8-bit formats.
For other streams (e.g. H.264 High 10 or HEVC Main 10, when the
hardware decoder cannot be used), GetFormat() fails with "no supported
pixel formats" once decoding has started, and no frame is shown.

Use the bit depth reported by the demuxer and fail Open() instead, so
that another decoder is used.
---
 .../DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp          | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
index fa51ed7..00b0176 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
@@ -302,6 +302,16 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::Open(CDVDStreamInfo& hints, CDVDCodecOptions& optio
     return false;
   }
 
+  // software decoded frames are only supported with 8 bits: leave the others
+  // to another decoder, as the error would only be noticed when decoding
+  if (!FindHWConfig(pCodec) && hints.bitdepth > 8)
+  {
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+              "CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::{} - {}-bit video is not supported by software decoding",
+              __FUNCTION__, hints.bitdepth);
+    return false;
+  }
+
   CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::{} - using decoder {}", __FUNCTION__,
             pCodec->long_name ? pCodec->long_name : pCodec->name);
 
